[[File:Red copyright.svg|25px|link=|Copyrighted]] Generally speaking, stamps are considered as organizational works ("work-for-hire"). Stamps issued before 1946 are acceptable for Commons; otherwise, not acceptable due to URAA restoration or regular 70-year copyright protection. Note that there could be exceptions, e.g., a derivative work of individual works.

==Threshold of originality== <!--T:61-->

</translate><noinclude>{{CRT shortcut|TOO|Japan}}
</noinclude><translate>
<!--T:62-->
Logos in the gallery below are {{OkMark}} to upload. 
Article 2 of Japanese copyright law defines that a work is eligible for copyright when it is a production in which thoughts or sentiments are expressed in a creative way and which falls within the literary, scientific, artistic or musical domain.</translate><ref name=Law1980/>
<translate>

<!--T:63-->
Japanese courts have decided that to be copyrightable, a text logo needs to have artistic appearance that is worth artistic appreciation. Logos composed merely of geometric shapes and texts are also not copyrightable in general. 
